  "answer": "For May support operations, the Import/OCR ticket count was **112** [NL-029#NL-029-S02][NL-012#NL-012-S07]. The documented root cause for these tickets is that customers upload **image-only or poorly scanned PDFs that lack native text layers**; NovaLearn’s ingestion pipeline relies on standard PDF text extraction, so such files fail to extract text, resulting in empty document indexes or garbled output [NL-029#NL-029-S02][NL-029#NL-029-S05]. The recommended operational response is to **develop a pre-ingestion scanning tool** in the KnowledgeHub admin dashboard that analyzes uploaded PDFs for text layers and warns users if a file is image-only before it enters the ingestion queue [NL-029#NL-029-S06]. Additionally, support agents currently advise customers to run external OCR tools before uploading, and a permanent resolution requires the release of the **Advanced OCR Pipeline** (planned for August 2026) [NL-029#NL-029-S05].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
